# 🔴 CHECK EVERY TEXT FILE OUT WITH LF, ON EVERY PLATFORM.
#
# `generator/generate-content.mjs` starts with a shebang. Cloned on Windows with
# the default `core.autocrlf=true`, that line becomes `#!/usr/bin/env node\r\n`,
# esbuild's shebang stripping no longer matches it, and importing the module
# fails with:
#
#     SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token
#
# Three suites import that generator, so all three fail to load and 99 tests
# silently stop running — with no hint that line endings are the cause.
# Reproduced in a clean Windows clone and fixed by converting the file to LF.
#
# Linux runners check out LF already, which is why CI never saw this and a
# Windows contributor would see nothing else. Declaring it here makes the
# working tree identical on both.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never translate these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.dump binary
*.sql.gz binary
